Task: Make purerest publishable as a real, versioned jar

Summary: Added sbt-dynver plugin (project/plugins.sbt) so purerest's version
is derived from git tags/commits rather than a manually-maintained val;
confirmed via `sbt purerest/version` (currently 0.0.0+263-74f2a41b+... since
no git tags exist yet). Set `purerest / organization := "io.github.beckfordp"`
in build.sbt, derived from this repo's own GitHub remote. Ran
`sbt purerest/publishLocal` and confirmed a real jar landed at
~/.ivy2/local/io.github.beckfordp/purerest_3/<version>/jars/purerest_3.jar.
Added scripts/verify-purerest-publish.sh to automate that check going
forward, and ran it (all checks passed).

Files changed: project/plugins.sbt, build.sbt, scripts/verify-purerest-publish.sh

Why: purerest needs a real Maven/Ivy coordinate and a real version to be
published as a jar at all — sbt's defaults (no organization, "0.1.0-SNAPSHOT")
aren't meaningful. Prep for the next backlog item (smoke-testing purerest as
an external libraryDependencies consumer) and the eventual real extraction.
order-service/inventory-service still consume purerest via ProjectRef, not
the published jar.
